WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
When I tell people that I'm on the debate team, I generally get one of two responses.

00:06.000 --> 00:10.000
The first being, I could never do that.

00:10.000 --> 00:18.000
The second, wow, people have always told me I would be great at debate. I love to argue.

00:18.000 --> 00:24.000
Well, both of these responses illustrate a real problem with how we view debate today.

00:24.000 --> 00:26.000
Debate is seen as a fight.

00:26.000 --> 00:33.000
If an argument is seen as a fight, then the winner is the person who can talk the loudest,

00:33.000 --> 00:37.000
who looks the prettiest on stage, or who can garner the most support.

00:37.000 --> 00:39.000
Yeah, debate is so much more than that.

00:39.000 --> 00:44.000
It's about who is the best speaker and who can illustrate their points the strongest.

00:44.000 --> 00:50.000
Now, this isn't all just a shameless plug to try and get you to join the debate team.

00:50.000 --> 00:52.000
But you should join.

00:53.000 --> 00:59.000
This is a shameless plug to get you to reevaluate the way you form an argument and an opinion,

00:59.000 --> 01:07.000
because real debate needs facts, logic, reasoning, and refutation to hold up.

01:07.000 --> 01:12.000
So, I'm going to tell you the story of the first time I remember losing a debate.

01:12.000 --> 01:18.000
So, I was with my mom and my younger sister in the car, or my older sister in the car,

01:18.000 --> 01:20.000
and we were driving home from school.

01:20.000 --> 01:26.000
And I told them what I learned that day, that Mount Everest is the tallest mountain in the whole world.

01:26.000 --> 01:28.000
My sister immediately shot me down.

01:28.000 --> 01:34.000
She said, actually, Mauna Kea in Hawaii is way taller than that.

01:34.000 --> 01:36.000
I started screaming at her.

01:36.000 --> 01:38.000
I said, no, you're wrong.

01:38.000 --> 01:41.000
A little spoiler alert, I was wrong.

01:42.000 --> 01:49.000
So, actually, Mauna Kea is a mountain in Hawaii, but it's like a volcano.

01:49.000 --> 01:54.000
And if you go below sea level, it's about a mile taller than Everest.

01:54.000 --> 01:55.000
I didn't know that at the time.

01:55.000 --> 02:01.000
And I had learned from my teacher that Mount Everest was the tallest, so I believed it.

02:01.000 --> 02:05.000
And I fought to defend that point, just with words.

02:05.000 --> 02:07.000
My sister would win, but in a fight.

02:07.000 --> 02:13.000
But I fought to get that point together, even though I didn't have all the information.

